On the tablet, retain the receiver for the session:

```kotlin
class SensorReceiver(ditto: Ditto) {
    // Keep the newest unread frame; never block the receive driver thread.
    val readings = Channel<ByteArray>(Channel.CONFLATED)
    private val streams = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet<DittoStream>()

    private val acceptor = ditto.dataStreams.bindTopic(
        topic = "sensor_data",
        reliability = DittoReliability.Unreliable,
    ) { candidate ->
        val stream = candidate.open { inbound ->
            readings.trySend(inbound.payload()) // payload() returns an owned copy
        }
        streams.add(stream)
    }

    // Call after stopping the session's other jobs.
    suspend fun shutdown() {
        acceptor.close()
        streams.toList().forEach { it.closeSync() }
        streams.clear()
        readings.close()
    }
}
```

Consume `readings` in a coroutine; decode there and dispatch UI work to Main. Opening inside the bind callback avoids retaining an expired candidate. If deferred opening is necessary, use `candidate.take()` inside the callback and `owned.use { ... }` in the coroutine; opening must happen while the connector is still waiting.

