Open `Ditto` once before `runApp` in an app-level service, and call `ditto.close()` only when the app shuts down. A better long-term setup is to move the observer into a repository that exposes a `ValueNotifier`, so widgets don't own Ditto handles. Don't put a `StreamBuilder` directly on `changes`: a rebuild throws `Stream has already been listened to.`

On 5.2.0, `ditto.store.observers` lists every V1 observer that hasn't been cancelled. You can use it to check that leaving this screen leaves none behind.

