Using the local `flutter-sdk` guidance, there are five issues:

- In 5.2.0, `onChange` also buffers results in the unlistened `changes` stream, causing memory growth.
- Discarding observer/subscription handles leaves them active.
- Closing the shared Ditto in `dispose()` causes other screens to throw `DittoClosedException`.
- `result.items` is an `Iterable`, not a `List`. Store plain maps/models instead of native result items.
- Sync subscriptions reject `ORDER BY` and `LIMIT` synchronously. As written, initialization throws before registering the observer; those clauses belong in the local observer query.

```dart
import 'dart:async';
import 'package:ditto_live/ditto_live.dart';
// Keep your existing Flutter imports.

class _InventoryState extends State<InventoryScreen> {
  List<Map<String, dynamic>> _items = [];

  late final SyncSubscription _syncSubscription;
  late final StoreObserver _observer;
  late final StreamSubscription<QueryResult> _changes;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();

    _syncSubscription = widget.ditto.sync.registerSubscription(
      'SELECT * FROM items',
    );

    _observer = widget.ditto.store.registerObserver(
      'SELECT * FROM items ORDER BY name LIMIT 100',
    );

    // Attach exactly one listener immediately; omit onChange.
    _changes = _observer.changes.listen((result) {
      if (!mounted) return;
      final items = result.items.map((item) => item.value).toList();
      setState(() => _items = items);
    });
  }

  @override
  void dispose() {
    // Flutter dispose cannot await. Cancel while Ditto is still open.
    unawaited(_changes.cancel());
    _observer.cancel();
    _syncSubscription.cancel();
    super.dispose();
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Text('${_items.length} items');
}
```

The app-level owner keeps Ditto open across screens and closes it only during shutdown, after resource cleanup. The observer limits displayed local results to 100; the sync subscription covers all items.

