On Flutter Web, Ditto 5.2.0 accepts **bytes, not file paths**. Use `file_picker` with `withData: true`, store the resulting `Attachment` in an `ATTACHMENT` field, then fetch its bytes for `Image.memory`.

Based on the installed Flutter SDK attachment guidance:

```dart
import 'dart:typed_data';
import 'package:ditto_live/ditto_live.dart';
import 'package:file_picker/file_picker.dart';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Future<void> pickAndSavePhoto(Ditto ditto, String id) async {
  final picked = await FilePicker.platform.pickFiles(
    type: FileType.image,
    withData: true,
  );
  if (picked == null) return;

  final file = picked.files.single;
  final bytes = file.bytes;
  if (bytes == null) throw StateError('No photo bytes returned');

  final attachment = await ditto.store.newAttachment(
    bytes,
    AttachmentMetadata({'name': file.name}), // positional argument
  );

  await ditto.store.execute(
    '''INSERT INTO COLLECTION photos (photo ATTACHMENT)
       DOCUMENTS (:doc) ON ID CONFLICT DO UPDATE''',
    arguments: {
      'doc': {'_id': id, 'photo': attachment},
    },
  );
}

Future<Uint8List> loadPhoto(Ditto ditto, String id) async {
  final result = await ditto.store.execute(
    '''SELECT * FROM COLLECTION photos (photo ATTACHMENT)
       WHERE _id = :id''',
    arguments: {'id': id},
  );
  if (result.items.isEmpty) throw StateError('Photo not found');

  final token =
      result.items.first.value['photo'] as Map<String, dynamic>;

  final fetcher = ditto.store.fetchAttachment(token, (_) {});
  final attachment = await fetcher.attachment;
  if (attachment == null) throw StateError('Photo unavailable');

  return await attachment.data;
}
```

In your widget, create and retain `photoFuture = loadPhoto(ditto, id)` outside `build`, then render:

```dart
FutureBuilder<Uint8List>(
  future: photoFuture,
  builder: (context, snapshot) {
    if (snapshot.hasError) return const Text('Could not load photo');
    if (!snapshot.hasData) return const CircularProgressIndicator();
    return Image.memory(snapshot.data!);
  },
)
```

The document contains an attachment **token**; another client must call `fetchAttachment` to download the bytes. Retain the fetcher and call `stop()` if the UI abandons an unfinished download.

