Using the local `flutter-sdk` guidance, there are five problems:

- In 5.2.0, `onChange` also buffers results in the unlistened `changes` stream, causing memory growth. Use one immediate `changes` listener.
- Discarding observer/subscription handles prevents proper cleanup.
- `result.items` is an `Iterable`, not a `List`. Store plain maps rather than native result objects.
- Closing the shared Ditto instance breaks other screens. Its app-level owner should close it at shutdown.
- Sync subscriptions reject `ORDER BY` and `LIMIT` synchronously, so this exact snippet fails before registering its observer. Apply those clauses to the local observer.

```dart
import 'dart:async';
import 'package:ditto_live/ditto_live.dart';
import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';

class _InventoryState extends State<InventoryScreen> {
  List<Map<String, dynamic>> _items = [];

  late final SyncSubscription _syncSubscription;
  late final StoreObserver _observer;
  late final StreamSubscription<QueryResult> _changes;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();

    _syncSubscription = widget.ditto.sync.registerSubscription(
      'SELECT * FROM items',
    );

    _observer = widget.ditto.store.registerObserver(
      'SELECT * FROM items ORDER BY name LIMIT 100',
    );

    _changes = _observer.changes.listen((result) {
      if (!mounted) return;
      final items = result.items.map((item) => item.value).toList();
      setState(() => _items = items);
    });
  }

  @override
  void dispose() {
    // Cancel screen-owned resources while the shared Ditto stays open.
    unawaited(_changes.cancel());
    _observer.cancel(); // V1 requires explicit observer cancellation.
    _syncSubscription.cancel();
    super.dispose();
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Text('${_items.length} items');
}
```

