Register it inside **`DisposableEffect`**, and close the returned handle in `onDispose`. This ties it to the screen’s composition lifetime.

```kotlin
@Composable
fun CarsScreen(ditto: Ditto) {
    var cars by remember { mutableStateOf(emptyList<String>()) }
    val query = "SELECT * FROM cars"

    DisposableEffect(ditto, query) {
        val observer = ditto.store.registerObserver(query) { result ->
            cars = result.items.map { it.jsonString() }
        }

        onDispose {
            observer.close()
        }
    }

    // Render cars…
}
```

Recomposition with unchanged keys keeps the observer; leaving composition closes it. Don’t register directly in the composable body, which can create duplicate observers.

